.TH PATCH 1 "2026" "KERNEL32" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
patch \- applique une difference a un fichier / apply a diff file to an original
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B patch
[-pN] [-R] [-N] [-b] [-s] [-F N] [--dry-run] [-d dir] [-i patchfile] [-o out] [file]
.br
.SH DESCRIPTION
Applies unified, context and normal diffs. Hunks are located by line offset with up to 2 lines of context tolerance (fuzz); rejected hunks go to file.rej. A
file whose old name is /dev/null is created, one whose new name is /dev/null is removed. A patch that is already applied is detected and skipped (use -N to
ignore this).
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B -pN
Strip N leading path components from file names.
.TP
.B -R
Reverse the patch.
.TP
.B -b
Keep the original as file.orig.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Check without changing files.
.TP
.B -F N
Maximum fuzz factor (default 2).
.SH SEE ALSO
diff(1)
